# title: Down-and-in put
# category: Barriers and touch options
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: A put that only comes to life if the stock closes at or below the barrier at some point.
# param: strike = 1.0 | percent | Strike, % of the initial level
# param: barrier = 0.7 | percent | Knock-in barrier, % of the initial level
#
# Daily closes. The building block of every barrier reverse convertible.

2027-01-04
    strike = 1.0
    barrier = 0.7
    s0 = spot()
    ki = 0

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() <= barrier * s0 then ki = 1 endIf

2028-01-04
    if spot() <= barrier * s0 then ki = 1 endIf
    if ki = 1 then pays max(strike * s0 - spot(), 0) endIf
